messages:
nina: Heads-up — the API ref example for PUT /models/{model_id}/rollout is stale. It shows "strategy": "canary" as a string but the runtime now expects an object with type/weight. This is tripping the generated TS and Go snippets.
josh: ah ok. which file/section?
nina: under "Responses & Examples" in the model rollout page. current example (old):
```json
{
  "model_id": "m-abc",
  "strategy": "canary",
  "targets": ["prod"]
}
```
The runtime accepts that for backwards compatibility but canonical request body shape is now: 
```json
{
  "model_id": "m-abc",
  "strategy": { "type": "canary", "weight": 20 },
  "targets": ["prod"]
}
```
Using the object enables percent-based rollouts and explicit type fields for future strategies. Our SDKs (TS/Go) were updated to reflect the object shape months ago which is why examples vs real responses are misaligned.
priya: agreed. recommendation: update the API ref example to use the object shape, add a one-line migration note: "legacy string strategy values are still accepted but will be deprecated; prefer strategy objects (type/weight)" and a link to the rollout SDK types. Also update the OpenAPI example and regenerate snippets.
kevin: we should also add a tiny code snippet showing client usage and type guard in TS, e.g.:
```ts
// types.ts
interface RolloutStrategyObj { type: 'canary' | 'linear' | 'bluegreen'; weight?: number }
interface RolloutReq { model_id: string; strategy: RolloutStrategyObj | string; targets: string[] }

const res = await client.models.rollout({ model_id: 'm-abc', strategy: { type: 'canary', weight: 20 }, targets: ['prod'] })
if (typeof res.request.strategy === 'string') {
  // legacy path
} else {
  // new structured path
}
```
nina: I've opened a draft docs PR with the change (updates example + adds migration note + OpenAPI example tweak): https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/721 (draft). Added a short changelog line for the migration guide too.
docs-bot: docs lint queued on PR #721 :eyes: (will fail if OpenAPI example still expects string)
priya: pinging infra to regenerate SDK snippets after the docs merge so examples in SDK readmes match.
deploy-bot: noted — we'll schedule snippet regen job after merge. Watch the snippet generator mapping for older clients that might still pass strings.
kevin: added unit test snippet to the PR showing both request shapes accepted by the runtime. helps reviewers.
josh: sounds good. let's also add a short note in the rollout API changelog section (date + breaking/compatible note). I can review the PR today.
nina: thanks — aiming to land by EOD tomorrow if CI is green. :thumbsup:
